                "text": "**Analyzing Shape Identification**\n\nI'm currently focused on discerning whether the primary shapes are 2x2 blocks or L-trominoes. My initial observation of the \"train 1\" input suggests L-trominoes, as the number '4' appears to occupy three cells and is adjacent to empty cells ('0'). The transformation of an empty cell to '3' in the output further supports this interpretation, indicating a connection between the shapes and the filling process.\n\n**Observing Shape Transformations**\n\nI'm refining my hypothesis. The inputs appear to be trominoes within 2x2 squares. The numbers 3 and 4 seem to represent specific tromino configurations, and the output fills the missing cell of the 2x2 square with the \"other\" number. I'm analyzing which tromino configuration leads to which fill color.\n\n**Confirming Complementary Colors**\n\nI've confirmed that in all training examples, the only non-zero colors present are 3 and 4, suggesting they are complementary. This pattern seems to hold true for the test input as well, where all existing shapes are color 4. My current hypothesis is that the missing cell in the 2x2 square will be filled with the complement color, which would be 3 in this case.\n\n**Testing Complementary Logic**\n\nI've been meticulously examining each 2x2 area in the test input. My verification confirms that when a tromino of color 4 is present, the missing cell within the 2x2 square is consistently filled with color 3. This reinforces the complementary color hypothesis.\n\n**Verifying Complementary Fills**\n\nI've been meticulously verifying each 2x2 area in the test input. My checks confirm that when a tromino of color 4 is present, the missing cell within that 2x2 square is consistently filled with color 3, solidifying the complementary color hypothesis.\n\n",
